{title: Pass Me Not o Gentle Savior}
{artist: Fanny Jane Crosby & William Howard Doane}
{key: G}

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]Pass me [C]not, O gentle [G]Savior,
[D]Hear my humble [G]cry;
while on [C]others thou art [G]calling,
[D]Do not [G/D]pass [D]me [G]by.

{comment: Chorus}
[G]Savior, [Am/C]Savior[C], [G]hear my humble [D]cry;
[G]While on [C]others thou art [G]calling,
[D]Do not [G/D]pass [D]me [G]by.

{comment: Verse 2}
Let me at thy throne of mercy
find a sweet relief,
kneeling there in deep contrition;
help my unbelief.

{comment: Verse 3}
Trusting only in thy merit,
would I seek thy face;
heal my wounded, broken spirit,
save me by thy grace.

{comment: Verse 4}
Thou the spring of all my comfort,
more than life to me,
whom have I on earth beside thee?
Whom in heaven but thee?
